W: 1. When I first came to town,
W: They called me "The Roving Jewel,"
W: Now they've changed their tune,
W: They call me "Katy Cruel,"
W: Oh, diddle, lully day,
W: Oh, de little lioday.
W:
W: Chorus:
W: Oh that I was where I would be,
W: Then I would be where I am not,
W: Here am I where I must be,
W: Go where I would, I can not,
W: Oh, diddle, lully day,
W: Oh, de little lioday.
W:
W: 2. When I first came to town,
W: They brought me the bottles plenty;
W: Now they've changed their tune,
W: They bring me the bottles empty,
W: Oh, diddle, lully day,
W: Oh, de little lioday.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 3. I know who I love,
W: And I know who does love me;
W: I know where I'm going,
W: And I know who's going with me,
W: Oh, diddle, lully day,
W: Oh, de little lioday.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 4. Through the woods I go,
W: And through the bogs and mire,
W: Straightway down the road,
W: And to my heart's desire,
W: Oh, diddle, lully day,
W: Oh, de little lioday.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 5. Eyes as bright as coal,
W: Lips as bright as cherry,
W: and 'tis her delight
W: To make the young girls merry,
W: Oh, diddle, lully day,
W: Oh, de little lioday.
W: (Chorus:)
W: (Repeat Verse 1 and Chorus)
